    "findings": [
      "All three reverse consumers use scalar common hash/modulo and no SIMD/gather or helper calls.",
      "Direct and checkpoint upper_bound comparison decisions lower to csel; loop exit branch only.",
      "Widths local prefix has a data-dependent exit per width plus its bounded-loop backedge. Hit path executes first four of seven instructions; miss path executes all seven.",
      "Direct16 hoists/caches both source extent uses per block; widths and direct32 retain one extra extent load per query, a compiler placement difference.",
      "Owners array stores are real consumer output; stack frames have 2048 B owners plus 48/64 B save area. No decoded endpoints or hot spills.",
      "Whole reverse timings do not isolate branch-miss, division latency or cache service."
    ]
